{
  "format": "wcoast-patch",
  "version": 1,
  "app": "DreamRack",
  "appVersion": "0.1.0",
  "rack": { "rows": 2 },
  "pages": [{ "id": "a1", "name": "Audio 1", "stops": [0, 0] }],
  "mixerPos": { "row": 1, "x": 0 },
  "modules": [
    { "id": "m0", "type": "coordinate-field", "page": "video", "row": 0, "x": 0 },
    { "id": "m1", "type": "shapes", "page": "video", "row": 0, "x": 81.28 },
    { "id": "m2", "type": "video-maths", "page": "video", "row": 0, "x": 121.92 },
    { "id": "m3", "type": "time-machine", "page": "video", "row": 0, "x": 162.56 },
    { "id": "m4", "type": "compositor", "page": "video", "row": 0, "x": 203.2 },
    { "id": "m5", "type": "video-out", "page": "video", "row": 0, "x": 243.84 },
    { "id": "m6", "type": "encoder", "page": "video", "row": 1, "x": 0 },
    { "id": "m7", "type": "chroma", "page": "video", "row": 1, "x": 40.64 },
    { "id": "m8", "type": "colorizer", "page": "video", "row": 1, "x": 81.28 }
  ],
  "wiring": [
    { "from": { "module": "m0", "port": "fieldOut" }, "to": { "module": "m1", "port": "fieldIn" } },

    { "from": { "module": "m0", "port": "fieldOut" }, "to": { "module": "m2", "port": "aIn" } },
    { "from": { "module": "m1", "port": "shapeOut" }, "to": { "module": "m2", "port": "bIn" } },
    { "from": { "module": "m2", "port": "outImage" }, "to": { "module": "m6", "port": "rIn" } },

    { "from": { "module": "m1", "port": "shapeOut" }, "to": { "module": "m6", "port": "gIn" } },

    { "from": { "module": "m1", "port": "shapeOut" }, "to": { "module": "m3", "port": "imageIn" } },
    { "from": { "module": "m3", "port": "imageOut" }, "to": { "module": "m6", "port": "bIn" } },

    { "from": { "module": "m6", "port": "imageOut" }, "to": { "module": "m7", "port": "imageIn" } },
    { "from": { "module": "m7", "port": "imageOut" }, "to": { "module": "m4", "port": "aIn" } },

    { "from": { "module": "m0", "port": "fieldOut" }, "to": { "module": "m8", "port": "imageIn" } },
    { "from": { "module": "m8", "port": "imageOut" }, "to": { "module": "m4", "port": "bIn" } },

    { "from": { "module": "m1", "port": "shapeOut" }, "to": { "module": "m4", "port": "keyIn" } },
    { "from": { "module": "m4", "port": "imageOut" }, "to": { "module": "m5", "port": "imageIn" } }
  ],
  "settings": {
    "params": {
      "m0": {
        "field": "radius",
        "scale": 0.64,
        "tile": 5.24,
        "quantise": 4.7,
        "twist": 0.42,
        "rotate": 0.27,
        "polar": 0.13,
        "scroll": 0.51
      },
      "m1": { "mode": "above", "width": 0.47, "centre": 0.11, "soft": 0.24 },
      "m2": { "op": "diff", "gainA": 1, "gainB": 1, "amount": 1 },
      "m3": { "mode": "trails", "depth": 0.62, "spread": 0.6, "mix": 1 },
      "m4": { "mode": "mix", "mix": 0.5, "key": 0.9 },
      "m6": { "gainR": 1, "gainG": 0.85, "gainB": 1.15 },
      "m7": { "hue": 0.12, "sat": 1.35, "level": 1, "contrast": 1.3 },
      "m8": { "palette": "heat", "spread": 1.4, "shift": -0.15, "cycle": 0 },
      "m5": { "test": "off" }
    }
  },
  "probes": [],
  "notes": "Video demo, in colour — where the reel-video demo ends, with the three colour modules added.\n\nThe monochrome half is unchanged: Coordinate Field on radius, quantised into bands, tiled, twisted and scrolling, with Shapes keeping everything above a slice of it.\n\nTwo routes to colour run side by side, which is the point of the patch.\n\nTHE ENCODER ROUTE — three chains that disagree. Red is the field and the shape met on Video Maths set to difference, so red lights only where the two disagree, which is the edges. Green is the shape itself. Blue is the shape through Time set to trails, so blue lags the other two and a moving shape drags a wake behind it. Because the three channels are genuinely different pictures, the edges come out coloured rather than grey — that is what an encoder is for, and no single chain produces it. Chroma then rotates the hue of the whole thing and pushes the saturation past unity.\n\nTHE COLORIZER ROUTE — one cable off the field, straight through the heat palette, with SPREAD opened up and SHIFT pulled back so the image reaches the whole of it. Smooth where the encoder route is edgy.\n\nThe Compositor crossfades between them with the SHAPE ITSELF as the key, so the blend is per pixel rather than one number for the frame: the shapes carry the palette and the encoder route fills the gaps between them.\n\nWorth turning: Colorizer CYCLE, which rotates the palette under a still picture and is the knob to put an LFO on; Chroma HUE, the same thing for the encoder route; Chroma SAT down to zero, which gives the picture in grey and keeps it a picture; the Encoder's three GAIN knobs, which set the balance between edges, shape and wake; and Compositor MIX to favour one route over the other.",
  "notesOpen": true
}
